      "description": "Watch Poland vs Bosnia & Herzegovina highlights and goals from UEFA Nations League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 25, 2026. The UEFA Nations League delivered a display of tactical discipline and defensive resilience as Poland hosted Bosnia and Herzegovina . Both sides struggled to break the deadlock in a match where every inch of the pitch was contested with immense physical commitment. A Cautious Opening Phase On September 25, 2026, in front of a crowd of 46,775, the match began with Poland looking to establish dominance through set-pieces. Sebastian Szymanski and Piotr Zielinski both delivered dangerous corners in the opening ten minutes, but the Bosnian defense stood firm. Robert Lewandowski was flagged offside early on, a sign of the frustration that would follow for the star striker. The first half was characterized by heavy midfield battles, leading to yellow cards for Jakub Kiwior and Zinedin Smajlovic as the referee worked hard to maintain control of the physical encounter. Tactical Adjustments and Rising Tension At the start of the second half, both managers sought to inject new energy into their lineups. Poland introduced Wiktor Nowak and Przemyslaw Frankowski , while Bosnia and Herzegovina brought on Amar Memic . Despite the changes, the balance of power remained perfectly split, with ball possession sitting at 50% for each team. The second period became increasingly fractious, with a flurry of bookings issued to Sead Kolasinac , Jan Bednarek , and Matty Cash . Even Bosnian coach Sergej Barbarez found himself in the book for dissent as the pressure of the occasion mounted. Late Drama and the Final Whistle As the clock ticked toward 90 minutes, the game finally opened up. Bosnia and Herzegovina threatened through a counter-attack that saw Ermin Mahmic fire wide, while at the other end, Piotr Zielinski forced a crucial save from the goalkeeper. In the dying moments of stoppage time, Jan Bednarek had a golden opportunity to snatch the win, but his header drifted wide of the target. Ultimately, the defenses reigned supreme, and the referee's final whistle confirmed a goalless draw that saw both nations share the points after a grueling battle."
